--- a/FORK.md
+++ b/FORK.md
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
 # Fork notes — type-ahead recursive search
 
 This is a fork of **Thunar 4.18.11** (upstream tag `thunar-4.18.11`, released
-2024-07-30) carrying one feature that upstream does not have:
+2024-07-30) carrying one feature that upstream does not have, plus a fix to
+the search it depends on:
 
 > Typing a printable character into a focused Thunar window immediately starts a
 > search for that text, the way Nautilus/GNOME Files does it — no `Ctrl+F` first.
@@ -37,6 +38,19 @@ subfolders according to the existing **Include subfolders** preference
   `misc-type-ahead-search` (xfconf `/misc-type-ahead-search`), default `TRUE`.
 * `thunar/thunar-preferences-dialog.c` — a **Search as you type** check box in
   *Preferences → Advanced → Search*, above *Include subfolders*.
+* `thunar/thunar-list-model.c` — recursive search made usable on slow
+  locations, which matters a great deal once typing starts one by itself:
+  * `thunar_list_model_search_folder()` walks the tree breadth-first through a
+    `GQueue` instead of recursing into each subdirectory inline, and commits
+    each folder's matches as soon as that folder has been read rather than
+    after its whole subtree — previously the matches in the folder you started
+    from were delivered last of all.
+  * `thunar_list_model_launch_search_job()` — a changed query waits
+    `THUNAR_SEARCH_START_DELAY` (250 ms) before crawling, so typing a word
+    starts one search instead of one per character.
+  * Searching a 1.4 TiB SMB share for `QCAD`: nothing on screen after 45 s
+    before, 16 hits after 5 s and 106 after 45 s afterwards. See
+    `../docs/06-search-performance.md`.
 
 ## What is deliberately left alone
 
diff --git a/thunar/thunar-list-model.c b/thunar/thunar-list-model.c
index 19c36b80b..8edb0d13f 100644
--- a/thunar/thunar-list-model.c
